IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa27-definitions`
IMPORT `coa27-transfer`

-- coa27-tests-transfer.l4: tests for coa27-transfer.l4 (ss 1253A to 1253F). Expected values are decided from the text and written
-- beside each assertion.

-- ---- s 1253A
#ASSERT `s 1253A the Secretary of State may request assistance, information or investigation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253A the Secretary of State may request assistance, information or investigation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1253A the Secretary of State may request assistance, information or investigation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1253B(3): need not take steps if (a) prejudice, (b) legal proceedings in the UK, (c) disciplinary action by a recognised supervisory body
#ASSERT `s 1253B(3) the Secretary of State need not take steps to comply with the request` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253B(3) the Secretary of State need not take steps to comply with the request` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253B(3) the Secretary of State need not take steps to comply with the request` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253B(3) the Secretary of State need not take steps to comply with the request` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) must take all necessary steps if requested by an approved third country competent authority
#ASSERT `s 1253B(1) the Secretary of State must take all necessary steps to comply with the request` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253B(1) the Secretary of State must take all necessary steps to comply with the request` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253B(1) the Secretary of State must take all necessary steps to comply with the request` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1A) a request for transfer of papers: act in accordance with s 1253D
#ASSERT `s 1253B(1A) the Secretary of State must act in accordance with section 1253D` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253B(1A) the Secretary of State must act in accordance with section 1253D` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) "Within 28 days following the date on which he receives the request": received 1 March 2027, the 28 days following run 2 March to 29 March
#ASSERT `s 1253B(2) the last day of the period of 28 days following the date of receipt` (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS Date 29 3 2027
#ASSERT `s 1253B(2) the Secretary of State has complied with subsection (2)` (Date 1 3 2027) (JUST (Date 29 3 2027)) (Date 15 4 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253B(2) the Secretary of State has complied with subsection (2)` (Date 1 3 2027) (JUST (Date 30 3 2027)) (Date 15 4 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253B(2) the Secretary of State has complied with subsection (2)` (Date 1 3 2027) (JUST (Date 2 3 2027)) (Date 15 4 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither done: still running at 29 March, run out at 30 March
#ASSERT `s 1253B(2) the Secretary of State has complied with subsection (2)` (Date 1 3 2027) NOTHING (Date 29 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1253B(2) the Secretary of State has complied with subsection (2)` (Date 1 3 2027) NOTHING (Date 30 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the regulative form: time 0 is the date of receipt; the act at time 28 is in time, at time 29 it is not
#TRACE `s 1253B(2) the Secretary of State must provide the assistance or notify the reasons` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Secretary of State` DOES `s 1253B provide the assistance or information required, or notify the reasons why not` AT 28

#TRACE `s 1253B(2) the Secretary of State must provide the assistance or notify the reasons` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Secretary of State` DOES `s 1253B provide the assistance or information required, or notify the reasons why not` AT 29

-- ---- s 1253C
#ASSERT `s 1253C(1) the Secretary of State must notify the relevant approved third country competent authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(1) the Secretary of State must notify the relevant approved third country competent authority` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(2) the authority is the relevant approved third country competent authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(2) the authority is the relevant approved third country competent authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(2) the authority is the relevant approved third country competent authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) the notification must include the name, and the reasons where eligibility has been withdrawn
#ASSERT `s 1253C(3) the notification must include the name of the person concerned` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(3) the notification must include the name of the person concerned` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1253C(3) the notification must include the reasons for the withdrawal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(3) the notification must include the reasons for the withdrawal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1253C(3) the notification must include the reasons for the withdrawal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) reasonable grounds for suspecting (a) a contravention and (b) that it took place on the territory of an equivalent or transitional third country
#ASSERT `s 1253C(4) the Secretary of State must notify the relevant approved third country competent authority of the suspicion` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(4) the Secretary of State must notify the relevant approved third country competent authority of the suspicion` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(4) the Secretary of State must notify the relevant approved third country competent authority of the suspicion` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(5) the authority is the relevant approved third country competent authority for the suspicion` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(5) the authority is the relevant approved third country competent authority for the suspicion` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(6) the notification must include the name of the person concerned and the grounds for the suspicion` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253C(6) the notification must include the name of the person concerned and the grounds for the suspicion` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1253D(1): must not be transferred unless the authority is approved and the transfer is made in accordance with s 1253DA, DB or DC
#ASSERT `s 1253D(1) the transfer to the third country competent authority is permitted` TRUE `s 1253D(1)(a) transfer by the Secretary of State (section 1253DA)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253D(1) the transfer to the third country competent authority is permitted` TRUE `s 1253D(1)(b) transfer by a statutory auditor with the approval of the Secretary of State (section 1253DB)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253D(1) the transfer to the third country competent authority is permitted` TRUE `s 1253D(1)(c) transfer by a statutory auditor for the purposes of investigation of an auditor (section 1253DC)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the authority is not an approved third country competent authority: barred even by a route that says "may transfer" (fork F-E)
#ASSERT `s 1253D(1) the transfer to the third country competent authority is permitted` FALSE `s 1253D(1)(c) transfer by a statutory auditor for the purposes of investigation of an auditor (section 1253DC)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- some other route
#ASSERT `s 1253D(1) the transfer to the third country competent authority is permitted` TRUE `s 1253D(1) some other route` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the route's conditions fail
#ASSERT `s 1253D(1) the transfer to the third country competent authority is permitted` TRUE `s 1253D(1)(a) transfer by the Secretary of State (section 1253DA)` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the route's answer is not covered
#ASSERT `s 1253D(1) the transfer to the third country competent authority is permitted` TRUE `s 1253D(1)(a) transfer by the Secretary of State (section 1253DA)` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) nothing authorises a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation
#ASSERT `s 1253D(3) the sections referred to in subsection (1) authorise the disclosure` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253D(3) the sections referred to in subsection (1) authorise the disclosure` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1253DD: express agreement of the authority responsible for the auditor of the subsidiary
#ASSERT `s 1253DD(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253DD(1) this section applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DD(1) this section applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DD(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DD(2) the transfer by the Secretary of State under section 1253DA must not take place` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253DD(2) the transfer by the Secretary of State under section 1253DA must not take place` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1253DD(2) the transfer by the Secretary of State under section 1253DA must not take place` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1253DD(3) the Secretary of State must not approve the transfer under section 1253DB` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253DD(3) the Secretary of State must not approve the transfer under section 1253DB` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1253DD(3) the Secretary of State must not approve the transfer under section 1253DB` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1253DA: transfer by the Secretary of State, if request made, papers relate to (a) securities issued in the third country or (b) a group issuing consolidated accounts there, and arrangements under s 1253E
#ASSERT `s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power ("may ..."), so a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, since JUST FALSE would read as "may not" (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q5)
#ASSERT `s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power ("may ..."), so a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, since JUST FALSE would read as "may not" (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q5)
#ASSERT `s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power ("may ..."), so a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, since JUST FALSE would read as "may not" (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q5)
#ASSERT `s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- barred by s 1253DD(2)
#ASSERT `s 1253DA(1) the Secretary of State may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1253DB
#ASSERT `s 1253DB(1) the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1253DB(1) the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power ("may ..."), so a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, since JUST FALSE would read as "may not" (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q6)
#ASSERT `s 1253DB(1) the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1253DB(1) the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power ("may ..."), so a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, since JUST FALSE would read as "may not" (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q6)
#ASSERT `s 1253DB(1) the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the approved third country competent authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) must not approve unless the three conditions are met: a failed condition is the text's no; all met is not said to be enough
#ASSERT `s 1253DB(2) the Secretary of State may approve the transfer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1253DB(2) the Secretary of State may approve the transfer` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DB(2) the Secretary of State may approve the transfer` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DB(2) the Secretary of State may approve the transfer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DB(2) the Secretary of State may approve the transfer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1253DC
#ASSERT `s 1253DC the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1253DC the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power ("may ..."), so a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, since JUST FALSE would read as "may not" (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q7)
#ASSERT `s 1253DC the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1253DC the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power ("may ..."), so a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, since JUST FALSE would read as "may not" (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q7)
#ASSERT `s 1253DC the statutory auditor may transfer the audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1253DE
#ASSERT `s 1253DE(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253DE(1) this section applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DE(1) this section applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DE(1) this section applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DE(2) the Secretary of State must participate in the inspection` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253DE(2) the Secretary of State must participate in the inspection` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DE(3) the inspection must be under the leadership of the Secretary of State` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253DE(3) the inspection must be under the leadership of the Secretary of State` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253DE(3) the inspection must be under the leadership of the Secretary of State` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1253E
#ASSERT `s 1253E(1) the Secretary of State may enter into the arrangements` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(1) the Secretary of State may enter into the arrangements` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1253E(1) the Secretary of State may enter into the arrangements` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- fields in order: (2) statement of reasons, (3)(a), (3)(b), (5)(a), (5)(b), (5)(c), (6)(a), (6)(b), (7A)(a), (7A)(b)
`s 1253E test arrangements: every term`           MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`s 1253E test arrangements: no statement of reasons` MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`s 1253E test arrangements: no limit on use (3)(a)` MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE
`s 1253E test arrangements: no comparable use limit (3)(b)` MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 1253E test arrangements: no confidentiality (5)(a)` MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 1253E test arrangements: no comparable confidentiality (5)(b)` MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 1253E test arrangements: no commercial protection (5)(c)` MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 1253E test arrangements: no right to refuse (6)(a)` MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 1253E test arrangements: no comparable right (6)(b)` MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 1253E test arrangements: no limit on the Secretary of State's disclosure (7A)(a)` MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s 1253E test arrangements: no limit on the authority's disclosure (7A)(b)` MEANS `s 1253E arrangements` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: every term` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: no statement of reasons` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: no limit on use (3)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: no comparable use limit (3)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: no confidentiality (5)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: no comparable confidentiality (5)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: no commercial protection (5)(c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: no right to refuse (6)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: no comparable right (6)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: no limit on the Secretary of State's disclosure (7A)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(2)-(7A) the arrangements contain the terms the section requires` `s 1253E test arrangements: no limit on the authority's disclosure (7A)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4) the functions, each meeting equivalent requirements of the 2016 Regulations
#ASSERT `s 1253E(4) the function is one of those functions` `s 1253E(4)(a) quality assurance functions (equivalent to regulation 9)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(4) the function is one of those functions` `s 1253E(4)(b) investigation or disciplinary functions (equivalent to regulations 5 to 8 and 10)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(4) the function is one of those functions` `s 1253E(4)(c) public oversight functions (equivalent to regulation 3)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(4) the function is one of those functions` `s 1253E(4)(a) quality assurance functions (equivalent to regulation 9)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(4) the function is one of those functions` `s 1253E(4) some other function` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (7) the cases
#ASSERT `s 1253E(7) the case is one mentioned` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(7) the case is one mentioned` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253E(7) the case is one mentioned` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1253F
#ASSERT `s 1253F the Secretary of State must publish on a website the name of the authority and the country or territory in which it is established` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253F the Secretary of State must publish on a website the name of the authority and the country or territory in which it is established` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253F the Secretary of State has met the duty to publish` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1253F the Secretary of State has met the duty to publish` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253F the Secretary of State has met the duty to publish` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1253F the Secretary of State has met the duty to publish` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
